tasks.description:
Fix dead CSS in `apps/client/src/index.css`: the `animate-tasks` utility class is referenced at 34 call sites across the client (confirmed via `grep -rln "animate-tasks" apps/client/src | wc -l`; call sites include `apps/client/src/layers/features/chat/ui/message/ThinkingBlock.tsx`, `apps/client/src/layers/features/mesh/ui/NamespaceGroupNode.tsx`, `apps/client/src/layers/features/settings/ui/ServerTab.tsx`, `apps/client/src/layers/features/settings/ui/TunnelDialog.tsx`, `apps/client/src/layers/features/tasks/ui/TaskTemplateGallery.tsx`, `apps/client/src/layers/features/tasks/ui/TasksPanel.tsx`) but no `@keyframes tasks` or `@utility animate-tasks` rule exists anywhere in the file — the pulse is silently dead.

Add, following the exact pattern already used for `animate-drain` at `apps/client/src/index.css:660-669` (a `@keyframes` block followed by an `@utility` block that sets `animation-name`, duration, timing-function, iteration-count):

```css
@keyframes tasks {
  0%,
  100% {
    opacity: 0.6;
    transform: scale(1);
  }
  50% {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: scale(1.02);
  }
}

@utility animate-tasks {
  animation-name: tasks;
  animation-duration: 1.6s;
  animation-timing-function: ease-in-out;
  animation-iteration-count: infinite;
}
```

Match the design-system's calm breathing band (1.6s cycle, subtle opacity/scale, mirroring the existing `@keyframes breathe` at `apps/client/src/index.css:628-639` which drives `.dorkbot-avatar` at a 3s cycle — `animate-tasks` should read as a faster, quieter cousin of that same breathe motion, not a new visual language). Do not touch any of the 34 call sites — they already reference `animate-tasks` by class name and will pick up the new keyframe automatically once it resolves. Verify visually: run `pnpm dev:dogfood`, open a session with `ThinkingBlock` visible (streaming assistant turn), and confirm the thinking indicator now pulses instead of sitting static. This is a one-focused-commit fix, independent of the touch-chips feature itself — safe to build in parallel with task 1.1.
